@SamuelEnglard

Perhaps! Anyone’s free to have a crack at any issue they find here unless the team’s actively assigned, and even then they just have to ask. It’s got a couple moving parts, but nothing impossible. 


For anyone coming from Windows land: the reason the existing solution (calling GetConsoleWindow and using the Shell APIs directly to set progress on the window) doesn’t work is that GetConsoleWindow is an absolute abomination of an API and we never should have let a windowless application access the window it just happened to be hosted in. Circumventing the console and telling the shell to paint progress isn’t even something we can detect; we need applications to move to a standards-compliant or, at the least, _quasi-_ standards-compliant, mechanism for setting progress.
